{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Go to your labors.</b> Rashi explained that the tribe of Levi was not enslaved, and so it is stated in the Midrash: for at the beginning, when he came upon them with crushing labor, with soft speech, as we expounded above, the tribe of Levi said: we are destined to engage in the labor of carrying for the Holy One, blessed be He; heaven forbid that we should perform any labor for this wicked man for any wage he may give us. And the Levites answered and all of them said that they do not know how to make bricks. And from that day forward he had no opening of the mouth to ask them for any matter of labor. And when Moses grew up and saw their labors, that they were enslaved all seven days of the week without any rest, he came to Pharaoh and said: is there any nation that can labor without any rest in the world? If they were to rest one day a week, know that their work would be superior and done well. He said to him: you have spoken well. Tell them to choose for themselves one day for rest. And a miracle was done for them, and they chose for themselves the day of Shabbat. And that is what Moses said to them regarding the observance of Shabbat: ראו כי ה' נתן לכם השבת etc. — for from the day you were in Egypt He gave you to choose Shabbat to rest upon it."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The phrase 'with soft speech, as we expounded above' reads כדדרשינן לעיל, referring back to an earlier midrashic discussion; the exact referent is not specified by the compiler."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:45.596688405Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}